A||||8||DR650SE||Check engine oil while engine hot or cold?||||1||
Z||000000||DR650SE||11-13-2001||10:21 AM||||I think I'm ganna cry, today i pulled into my drive way and on the ground were some oil patches it looked.  I checked the brake fluid and it was full checked engine oil and it looked like it had none in it.  DAMN!  THe engine was hot when I checked.  Does that matter?  THe oil psi went low when i made sharp turns and sometimes not so sharp turns.  Did i damage anything?<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierocritter||11-13-2001||10:26 AM||||You can check your engine oil hot or cold and there won't a variation. When turning corners your oil was moving to one side of the oil pan not letting the oil pump pick the oil up. Do an oil change and fill to proper level than go from there!||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||11-13-2001||10:41 AM||||I usually check mine about 5 min after I shut it off. Oil still warm. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DR650SE||11-13-2001||10:58 AM||||Thanks for the info||||reg||11
Z||000004||btoth||11-13-2001||12:34 PM||||If you look in the serivce manual, it says check it cold.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  But then again, when you go to get an oil change, they obviously do it hot.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DR650SE||11-13-2001||12:38 PM||||Im ganna change the oil myself.  How many quarts exactly do I put in? Also what do I do with the old oil?<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000006||DR650SE||11-13-2001||12:38 PM||||Do I use 5w-30 or what?||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||11-13-2001||03:06 PM||||depends on the winter temps where you are, miles on engine. I use 10w40 in my other cars in winter in Ohio. My kitcar w/ turbo, I use 5w50 synthetic year round.||||reg||1
